    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with a aggressive posture on the basepaths, prioritizing high-upside speed threats despite a slate of challenging matchups. **Corbin Carroll** (77.89) stands as our premier play; despite a minor penalty for facing an elite catcher, his matchup against Blade Tidwell remains our highest-scoring start due to his projected elite contribution to both speed and power. **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) follows closely as the day's primary value beneficiary, leveraging a massive +14% boost from a favorable platoon matchup against Grant Holmes, while **Seiya Suzuki** (74.00) rounds out the outfield core, capitalizing on a \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor that increases the efficiency of his scoring potential against Rhett Lowder.\n\nThe bench decision process was disciplined, with **Josh Naylor** (50.39) serving as the most difficult cut. While **Josh Naylor** offered a respectable baseline, the optimizer prioritized the higher-leverage platoon and park advantages of our active starters; facing Dylan Cease and his 3.01 xERA ultimately suppressed **Josh Naylor**\u2019s ceiling, pushing him below the threshold required to crack our utility or corner spots. We also continue to monitor the status of **James Wood**, who remains stashed on the IL. Risk management remains critical today as all lineup slots are currently pending official verification. We are especially wary of the bottom-of-the-order slots like **Austin Riley** (63.42) and **Jose Caballero** (69.06); while their individual scores are strong, their projected positions (#8 and #9) introduce significant volatility that could dampen their counting stat production if their respective games do not follow the expected offensive script.",
